        {
          "say": "Calculator only where it says so. Work out angles with reasons, don't measure.",
          "write": "reasons, not rulers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Integers",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Subtracting a negative means adding. Minus 7 plus 12 plus 5 is 10.",
          "write": "−7 + 12 − (−5) = 10",
          "draw": {
            "type": "numberline",
            "from": -8,
            "to": 12,
            "start": 5,
            "jump": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Negative divided by negative is positive.",
          "write": "−24 ÷ (−3) = 8"
        },
        {
          "say": "Substitute with brackets. Minus 3, squared, is 9, not minus 9.",
          "write": "2(−3)² − 3(−4) = 30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Angles",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "On parallel lines look for F, Z and C shapes.",
          "write": "F, Z, C",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/year-8-semester-1-review-sa-parallel.svg",
          "alt": "Parallel lines with a 68 degree angle and angle x"
        },
        {
          "say": "180 take 68 is 112. That's angles on a straight line.",
          "write": "180° − 68° = 112°"
        },
        {
          "say": "x is corresponding to it, so x is 112 degrees.",
          "write": "x = 112° (corresponding)"
        },
        {
          "say": "A regular octagon. Exterior angles are 360 over 8, which is 45.",
          "write": "360° ÷ 8 = 45°"
        },
        {
          "say": "So each interior angle is 180 take 45, which is 135.",
          "write": "180° − 45° = 135°"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fractions and percentages",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Dividing fractions? Keep, change, flip.",
          "write": "7/3 × 4/7 = 4/3 = 1⅓"
        },
        {
          "say": "240 dollars up 15 percent is 276. Then down 15 percent.",
          "write": "240 × 1.15 = 276"
        },
        {
          "say": "276 times 0.85 is 234.60. Not back to 240!",
          "write": "276 × 0.85 = $234.60",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
            "alt": "Up 15 percent then down 15 percent ends below $240",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 400,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "$240"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 130,
                "w": 460,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "green",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "$276"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 200,
                "w": 391,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "$234.60"
              },
              {
                "kind": "line",
                "x": 440,
                "y": 40,
                "x2": 440,
                "y2": 270,
                "color": "red",
                "dashed": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "The decrease is 15 percent of a bigger amount, so it takes off more.",
          "write": "up then down ≠ no change"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Pythagoras and cylinders",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "x is the hypotenuse. Add the squares. 81 plus 144 is 225.",
          "write": "x² = 9² + 12² = 225",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/year-8-semester-1-review-sa-pythagoras.svg",
          "alt": "Right triangle with sides 9 and 12 and hypotenuse x"
        },
        {
          "say": "The square root of 225 is 15 centimetres.",
          "write": "x = 15 cm"
        },
        {
          "say": "Cylinder, radius 5, height 8. Pi times 25 times 8 is 200 pi.",
          "write": "V = 200π ≈ 628.3 cm³",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y8/maths/year-8-semester-1-review-sa-cylinder.svg",
          "alt": "Cylinder radius 5 cm height 8 cm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Algebra and index laws",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Expand. Minus 3 times minus 5 is plus 15.",
          "write": "4(2x − 3) − 3(x − 5)"
        },
        {
          "say": "Collect like terms. 5x plus 3.",
          "write": "= 5x + 3",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 230,
            "alt": "Collecting the x terms and numbers",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
